From: Gnoblin maintainers
Subject: Keep managed layer-shell stacking unchanged on pointer crossing

Mutter raises ordinary dock windows on pointer entry and exit. Layer-shell
surfaces use the dock type too, but their order must survive motion across
overlapping panels. Exclude only managed layer surfaces; retain ordinary dock
hover promotion, explicit layer keyboard acquisition and click-to-raise.

diff --git a/src/core/display.c b/src/core/display.c
index de19d57b0c..acdad694f5 100644
--- a/src/core/display.c
+++ b/src/core/display.c
@@ -3685,7 +3685,12 @@ meta_display_handle_window_enter (MetaDisplay *display,
       break;
     }
 
-  if (window && window->type == META_WINDOW_DOCK)
+  /* Layer-shell surfaces have a protocol-defined layer. Promoting them on
+   * pointer entry or exit can cover another panel before its input arrives.
+   * Keep the historical hover promotion for ordinary docks only; layer-shell
+   * still uses explicit keyboard acquisition and ordinary click-to-raise. */
+  if (window && window->type == META_WINDOW_DOCK &&
+      !g_object_get_data (G_OBJECT (window), "gnoblin-layer-surface"))
     meta_window_raise (window);
 }
 
